window.docContents[229].resolve({"/Abstraction/Properties/#Core-C______--Abstraction--Properties":{"contents":"A well typed program has a derivation, or is stuck at a case C++17 leaves undefined, which the evaluator reports as error. Every well typed constructor has an evaluation rule, checked by inspection of the rule set. There is no Lean proof, and the property is stated without proving it.\n\nEvery construction has rules with mutually exclusive premises, and a Core C++ program has at most one result. The evaluation order fixed left to right removes the choice C++17 leaves to the compiler. The relations of  make the statement precise, two derivations of  for the same  give the same  and , and there is no Lean proof yet.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Abstraction","header":"5.6. Properties","id":"/Abstraction/Properties/#Core-C______--Abstraction--Properties"}});